    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\nI implemented the rule by adding a step to the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline:\n\n- **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 a new function that runs before `BuildOwner`, counts existing owners in the requested city (using the same same-city equality as `AssignCustomerCode`), and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked) + **`CityAtCapacityHandler`** \u2014 the handler responds **409 Conflict**, wired via the escalation YAML `\u2026CityAtCapacityException.yml`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `rejectCityAtCapacity` between `rejectDuplicateHousehold` and `build`, so the rejection happens before the entity is built/saved (and the owner being created isn't counted).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
